Democrats and Republicans liberals and  conservatives all agree we've got to cut  large chunks of government spending over  the next decade or else we've got to  start learning how to speak Greek the  Congressional Budget Office projects  that if we keep spending the way we have  been federal debt held by the public  will grow from around sixty percent of  GDP to a whopping eighty two percent  conservative Republicans are happy to  talk about cutting spending on the poor  on education and even on cowboy poetry  readings but they insist that spending  on defense not only not be trimmed but  that it be increased here are three  reasons conservatives and all other  red-blooded Americans should cut defense  spending now  didn't we just win or at least end the  war in Iraq and aren't we winding down  in Afghanistan after world war two  Vietnam and the end of the Cold War  military spending got cut as it should  more to the point spending on the  military and homeland security has grown  by 90 percent in inflation-adjusted  dollars since 2000 if al Qaeda and most  international terrorist groups have been  largely vanquished we should not just be  bringing the troops home but the dollars  - unless that is conservatives want to  seriously argue that nearly doubling  outlays for the past decade haven't  yielded results that would allow us to  dial down defense spending the United  States already accounts for about 45  percent of the planet's military outlays  more than the next 14 countries combined  it's a conservative truism that  government programs even ones that are  sanctioned by the Constitution tend to  be bloated inefficient and incompetent  surely that logic applies to the  Pentagon in the Department of Homeland  Security in fact after spending fifty  six billion dollars in security measures  flying is no safer now than it was  before the 9/11 attacks  it was a republican president the war  here at Dwight Eisenhower who sounded  the alarm about the military industrial  complexes insidious ability to grow and  grow like a cancer on the American body  politic Americans are rightly tired not  just the dubious inconclusive wars that  have led to the death of thousands of  Americans and hundreds of thousands of  others they're all so tired of  out-of-control spending by a Washington  elite that is totally out of touch with  everyday Americans if conservatives want  to push forward on reducing spending on  Medicaid and other domestic programs  they should show that they take their  own limited government philosophy  seriously by pushing for defense cuts  between now and the 2012 elections for  reason TV I'm Nick Gillespie
 

